Suppose the PR description says 'Added retry logic for payment calls' and the diff includes:
```
import requests
from retrying_utils import retry_forever

@retry_forever
def charge(order):
    return requests.post(PAYMENT_URL, json=order.to_dict())
```
Questions to ask: does the library 'retrying_utils' actually exist, is it a dependency, is it maintained, and does it have the claimed function? Retrying forever with no limit or backoff can hammer the payment provider and double-charge if the first call succeeded but timed out, so is the call idempotent (an idempotency key)? There is no timeout on the request, no logging, and no test shown. Also check whether the diff touched files unrelated to the ticket.
